This is a more challenging problem. The queue data structure has several operations such as enqueue and dequeue that need to be implemented efficiently. We will use two stacks to achieve this. The idea is to use one stack for storing the elements in the order they are inserted, and another stack to store the elements in the reverse order. When an element needs to be dequeued, we simply pop the element from the second stack and return it. This approach has a space complexity of O(n) since both stacks will contain n elements after inserting n elements into the queue. 
